  "body": "**The request (mkinney, 2026-11-15):** a docs review for the next release, filed while the v0.21.0 cut (#1936) runs. It follows the \"file the next docs review at every release\" proposal in #1792. The site is built from the tagged tree at each release (AGENTS.md \"A cut goes PR review -> merge to main -> tag\", step 5), so docs merged now ship with v0.22.0.\n\n## Scope\n\n#1792 (PR #1802, merged 2026-11-15T06:13:51Z) reviewed the guide against the PRs merged up to then. **46 PRs merged after it** (count at filing time). They went into v0.21.0 without a guide review. For example:\n- Sodick wire EDM: the angle-word refusal (#1787), the ALC400G machine file (#1793), the 4-axis cut and flushing words when they land (#1497, #1499).\n- Sinker EDM body electrode (#1811). Stock carried into a side-on setup (#1804). 3D operations in aligned setups (#1858).\n- 2D: Adaptive Trochoidal controls (#1782) and parallel lanes (#1788). Bore clears wide holes with rings (#1839). U-shaped blind slot (#1841).\n- Explain G-code option for the Tormach and Fanuc posts (#1812, #1814). Setup-change stop names the next setup (#1859).\n- STEP import subdivision bounds (#1837), and anything else user-visible since #1802.\n\n## What to do\n\n1. List the PRs merged after #1802 (`gh pr list --state merged --search \"merged:>=2026-11-15T06:13:51Z\"`). Mark each one that changes what a user sees or does. Read its `Changelog:` line.\n2. Update the matching guide page, or add one. Pay special attention to:\n   - `operations-2d.md` (Adaptive Trochoidal, Bore rings, slots), `operations-3d.md` (aligned setups), `operations-edm.md` (Sodick, sinker electrode);\n   - `posting.md` (Explain G-code option), `machines.md` (Sodick ALC400G), `refusals.md` (the new refusal messages), `setups.md` (side-on carry, setup-change stop).\n3. If #1903 (regroup the guide) has merged, follow its new structure.\n4. `zola build` passes with no broken links. Screenshots come from CamCraft only (#1902), never committed review artifacts (#1794, #1845).\n\n## Done means\n\nEvery user-visible change merged after #1802 is in the guide, or a comment lists it as \"no doc needed\" with the reason. `zola build` passes. At the next cut, file the \"Docs review for v0.23.0\" issue the same way.\n",
